--- a/project/app/uvc_app_tiny/uvc_app/uvc/uvc_process.cpp
+++ b/project/app/uvc_app_tiny/uvc_app/uvc/uvc_process.cpp
@@ -1,6 +1,20 @@
 /*
  * Copyright (C) 2019 Rockchip Electronics Co., Ltd.
  *
+ * Patch 0002: uvc-process-venc-only-restart
+ *
+ * Problem:
+ *   On every streamon/streamoff cycle (including host-triggered resolution
+ *   changes), stopProcess() was tearing down VI, VPSS, and VENC together.
+ *   startProcess() then tried to re-initialise all three. Because uvc_vi_stop
+ *   is a no-op (patch 0001), VI stayed running — but the subsequent
+ *   startProcess() call attempted to re-bind an already-bound VI→VENC path,
+ *   causing RK_MPI_SYS_Bind to return an error and the pipeline to stall.
+ *
+ *   Additionally, stopProcess() for the VI_VENC path called unBindViVenc()
+ *   then immediately stopped VENC, which is correct, but startProcess() then
+ *   re-called startVi() which hit the broken DisableChn logic (now fixed in
+ *   patch 0001 — but we still must not re-bind a live VI channel).
+ *
+ * Fix:
+ *   Introduce a per-process flag `mViEverStarted` that tracks whether VI has
+ *   completed its first-time start. On subsequent startProcess() calls in the
+ *   VI_VENC and VI_VPSS_VENC paths, skip startVi() and go straight to
+ *   recreating VENC (and VPSS if needed). The bind path is also guarded: we
+ *   only bind VI→VENC when VI was freshly started this cycle.
+ *
